  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.0",
  "name": "Zyda",
  "identifier": "10.57967/hf/2394",
  "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\tZyda\n\t\n\n\n\nZyda is a 1.3T language modeling dataset created by collecting open and high quality datasets and combining them and performing a uniform filtering and deduplication step. We find that Zyda performs extremely well in ablations and is at least comparable and potentially better to the best openly available datasets available, due to our meticulous post-processing pipeline. We think the best use of Zyda is either as a standalone dataset for language model training up to the 1T\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Zyphra/Zyda.",
  "alternateName": [
    "Zyphra/Zyda",
    "Zyda"
  ],
  "creator": {
